%I A081419 #24 Nov 16 2026 17:15:34
%S A081419 0,1,2,3,4,6,9,34
%N A081419 Largest value held in any register at the end of a halting computation by an n-instruction register Minsky machine.
%C A081419 We start with initially empty registers and include exactly one Halt instruction. Analogous to the Busy Beaver function, Sigma, for Turing Machines.
%C A081419 a(9) >= 520 and a(10) > 2.64*10^73. - _Zhuorui He_, Nov 09 2026
%H A081419 bbchallenge, <a href="https://wiki.bbchallenge.org/wiki/Register_machine">Register machine</a>.
%H A081419 Tibor Rado, <a href="https://gwern.net/doc/cs/computable/1962-rado.pdf">On Non-Computable Functions</a>, Bell System Technical Journal, vol. 41, #3, 877-884, May 1962.
%F A081419 Noncomputable.
%e A081419 A program for a(3)=2 is:
%e A081419   1: A+ -> 2
%e A081419   2: A+ -> 3
%e A081419   3: HALT
%e A081419 which halts with A=2.
%e A081419 From _Sean A. Irvine_, Oct 28 2025: (Start)
%e A081419 A program for a(6)=6 is:
%e A081419   1: A+ -> 2
%e A081419   2: A+ -> 3
%e A081419   3: A+ -> 4
%e A081419   4: B- -> 6, 5 (jump to 5 is B=0, otherwise 6)
%e A081419   5: B+ -> 1
%e A081419   6: HALT
%e A081419 which halts with A=6.
%e A081419 A program for a(7)=9 is:
%e A081419   1: B+ -> 2
%e A081419   2: B+ -> 3
%e A081419   3: A+ -> 4
%e A081419   4: A+ -> 5
%e A081419   5: A+ -> 6
%e A081419   6: B- -> 3, 7
%e A081419   7: HALT
%e A081419 which halts with A=9. (End)
%Y A081419 Cf. A028444, A401603.
%K A081419 hard,nice,nonn,more,changed
%O A081419 1,3
%A A081419 Rick J. Griffiths (rjg42(AT)cam.ac.uk), Apr 20 2003
%E A081419 Conjectured a(9) removed by _Zhuorui He_, Nov 09 2026
